meta {
  name: Get Application Prefill
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/prefill
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Pre-fill data for a student starting their NEXT application, taken from
  their previous applications (any college/cycle). Call this on the
  Start Application screen, before Start Application — no applicationId
  needed.

  Response `data`:

  {
    hasPreviousApplication: boolean,
    sourceApplicationId: string | null,   // most recent previous application
    nationality: string | null,
    state_of_domicile: string | null,
    passport_country: string | null,
    passport_number: string | null,
    profile_photo_url: string | null,
    whatsapp_country_code: string | null,
    whatsapp_number: string | null,
    entrance_exam_details: { exams: [...] } | null
  }

  nationality/state_of_domicile/passport_* come from the most recent
  previous application. profile_photo_url, whatsapp_* and
  entrance_exam_details each come from the most recent previous
  application that has them set. All fields are null when
  hasPreviousApplication is false.

  The remaining form sections (personal/family/address/qualification/
  academic records/achievements) don't need this endpoint — they live on
  the Student profile and Get Application Form Details already returns
  them for every application. Declaration is never pre-filled.
}
